{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Patchset 2 — review-driven hardening of the new knob\n\nCode review on patchset 1 returned `LLM-Review +1` with three advisory findings. One is a genuine footgun in the knob this change introduces, so patchset 2 acts on it rather than resolving it away.\n\n**`free_watermark_pct` had no upper bound.** It is headroom to *keep free*, but `80` reads naturally as \"reclaim at 80% used\" — the inverse. Reproduced on a 30-GiB volume:\n\n| pct | trigger | | \n|---|---|---|\n| 20 | 6.00 GiB free | intended |\n| 80 | 24.00 GiB free | `free < trigger` true at every plausible level |\n| 100 | 30.00 GiB free | **trigger >= the whole volume** |\n\nAt 80 or above every pass evicts the entire store and every gate re-materializes its snapshot from scratch; at >=100 the trigger exceeds the volume outright. Since the docs added by this same change tell operators to set the knob, shipping that range would introduce a new defect. Patchset 2 clamps to `MAX_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT = 50` — clamped rather than rejected, because a janitor must never fail a gate over a tunable.\n\nVerified RED first (`AssertionError: the trigger must never demand the whole volume be free`), then GREEN. A second new test covers the reviewer's third finding — that `max()` was only exercised in the direction where the volume-relative term dominates; on a 10-GiB volume with `pct=10` the 2-GiB absolute floor correctly wins. That one passed unchanged, so it was a coverage gap, not a bug.\n\nThe second finding (`_snapshot_int` can now `KeyError` on a defaults mapping missing the key) is left as-is: the helper is private to `_config_sources.py`, its only caller passes the complete mapping built by `_default_tunables()`, and a missing key there is a programming error that should fail loudly rather than silently resolve to a wrong default.\n\nRe-verified on patchset 2: 26/26 in `tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py`, the exact-defect mutation still returns the original four cases to RED, the incident replay still reclaims at 82% (below the 85% floor), `make lint` + `make typecheck` green, complexity ratchet `new=0 increased=0`, and the full `tests/unit` suite passed locally on patchset 1's tree.\n\nNote: the amend regenerated the `Change-Id` and briefly opened a duplicate (change 1923). The original id was restored so this is **patchset 2 of [change 1922](https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1922)**, and 1923 is abandoned. The stale `LLM-Review +1` was dropped by the new patchset, as expected; both gates are re-running."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787179030426943001,"uuid":"6a9c6273-18fe-417b-8d84-a62a14dd6915"}